[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `\n`, `\v`, `\f`, `\r`) as skippable. Covered by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `scanf_reads_across_newlines`; the mutant that narrows the whitespace set to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m space only is caught by 4 tests.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Conversion failure leaves `x` at 0, and the program still exits 0
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `scanf`'s return value is discarded. On input failure (EOF first) or matching
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m failure (first non-whitespace byte cannot begin an integer) nothing is stored,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `x` stays 0, and the program prints `300` and exits 0. There is no error
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m message and no non-zero exit status on any input. So `""`, `"abc"`, `"-"`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `"."`, `"_5"`, `"\x005"` and whitespace-only input all print `300`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `\0` is worth calling out: it is neither whitespace nor a digit, so `"\x005"`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is a matching failure and prints `300`, not `310`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### `%d` stops at the first non-digit, mid-token
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `"1.5"` reads 1, `"0x10"` reads 0 and stops at the `x`, `"5e3"` reads 5,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `"12abc"` reads 12. Only the first conversion is performed; the rest of stdin
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is never read.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Two independent overflow points
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `2*x + 300` is computed in 32-bit `int` and wraps. `x = 1073741824` prints
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `-2147483348`; `x = INT_MAX` prints `298`. Signed overflow is undefined in C,
